===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ja|mure}}
{{ja-kanjitab|むれ|yomi=i|alt=牟礼}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}, itself apparently a borrowing from {{der|ja|oko|-|sort=むれ}}.<ref name="DJR"/><ref name="KDJ2-mure">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|牟礼・山}}</ref><ref name="DDJS">{{R:Digital-Daijisen}}</ref> See {{cog|ko|뫼}} for more.

The phonetic {{w|man'yōgana}} spelling {{m|ja|牟礼}} for ''mure'' appears first in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 720 {{CE}}, but instead for the stem of verb {{m|ja|群れる|tr=mureru||to group together}}.<ref name="KDJ2-mureru">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|群}}</ref> The first instance of this spelling for the {{m|en|mountain}} sense is in the {{w|Heian period}}, in different {{m|ja||{{w|lang=ja|日本書紀私記}}|tr=Nihon Shoki Shiki}} versions, themselves [[recompilation]]s of the ''{{w|Nihon Shoki}}''.<ref name="KDJ2-mure"/> This reading with this sense apparently arises from the traditional {{m|ja|訓読|tr=kundoku}} of a particular section of the ''{{w|Nihon Shoki}}'', where the written word {{m|ja|山}} is read as ''mure'' with an apparent meaning of {{m|en|mountain}} or {{m|en|hill}}.<ref name="KDJ2-mure"/><ref name="DJR-mure">{{R:Daijirin}}, entry online [https://web.archive.org/web/20201024122313/https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%B1%B1%E3%83%BB%E7%89%9F%E7%A4%BC-395079 here]</ref>

