===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|みさき|yomi=k|alt=崎,碕:rare}}
{{wp|ja:}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}.  First attested in the ''{{w|Nihon Shoki}}'' of 720.<ref name="KDJ2">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|岬・崎・碕}}</ref>

Analyzable as a compound of {{ja-com|み|み|pos1=see below|先|さき|t2=[[tip]], [[point]]; [[promontory]]}}.<ref name="KDJ2"/><ref name="DDJS">{{R:Digital-Daijisen}}</ref><ref name="K">{{R:Kojien}}</ref><ref name="M">{{R:Meikyo}}</ref><ref name="DJR"/><ref name="SMK5"/> 

The ''mi'' prefix is likely the honorific prefix {{ja-r|御|み-}}, and the term ''misaki'' is attested explicitly with the spelling {{ja-r|御%碕|み%-さき|linkto=-}} in the ''{{w|Nihon Shoki}}''.<ref name="KDJ2"/>

Alternative theories as to the identity of the {{ja-r|み}} include: <!-- Needs a ref — should this also be the KDJ2? -->
* {{ja-r|水|み|[[water]]|pos=bound prefix form of {{ja-r|水|みず}}}}, although the semantics this suggests may instead mean “water tip”, i.e. a jutting-out of water, not of land — an inlet.
* Shift from {{ja-r|海|うみ|[[sea]]}}, with the same consideration as above.

